CORE
negative-part-select-base1.sv
--bound 1
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.v\[-1\+:2\] !== 2'b11: PROVED up to bound 1$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
1800-2017 11.5.1: the base of an indexed part-select may evaluate to a
negative value.  Bits of the selected range that fall outside the
vector bounds read as x (4-state); this is not an error.  v[-1 +: 2]
selects out-of-range bit -1 (x) and in-range bit 0 (1), so the result
is not 2'b11.  EBMC handles this case correctly.
